Finding: the posted classification's site-count (6) and reasoning cover only the
5 build()-level boolean reads + the one onPressed call. Six additional, distinct
call sites in _googleLogin/_facebookLogin/_appleLogin/_processSocialSuccessSetup
(lines 216, 243, 270, 271, 289, 333) are not enumerated or individually
classified anywhere in Jira comment 18214 or the solution doc, despite AC1
requiring "every Get.find<XController>() call site in that file is read and
classified."

QA independently walked all 6 omitted sites: every one sits inside an async
event-handler method (_googleLogin/_facebookLogin/_appleLogin/_processSocialSuccessSetup),
never inside build() or any other render path — so by the ticket's own predicate
("a call site outside build() ... triggers an action or a one-time decision, not
paint — so it is (a) by construction") they are ALL correctly (a) too. The
ultimate 0-(b) conclusion for this file is NOT falsified, and the zero-code-change
outcome (AC3/AC4) remains correct. This is a completeness/documentation gap in
the posted AC1 record, not a missed stale-render bug.

Other 6 files checked for the same site-count pattern (raw grep vs claimed):
  social_login_widget.dart:        claimed ~14, actual 18   (within stated "~")
  order_info_widget.dart:          claimed 15,  actual 15   (exact match)
  VendorApp splash_screen.dart:    claimed ~13, actual 14   (within stated "~")
  VendorApp dashboard_screen.dart: claimed ~7,  actual 9    (within stated "~")
  DeliveryApp dashboard_screen.dart: claimed ~14, actual 20 (within ticket's own
                                     cited "~14-20" range; doc's own "~14" is low end)
  DeliveryApp my_account_screen.dart: claimed ~11, actual 12 (within stated "~")

login_suggestion_bottomsheet.dart is the only file with a materially wrong
count (6 claimed vs 18 live sites, ~3x) and the only one where distinct call
sites are entirely absent from the reasoning text rather than just under an
approximate tilde-count.
